{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-isovector-chiral-residue","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:isovector-chiral-residue","kind":"proposition","title":"Binding isovector coefficient as the $W_\\lambda$ chiral residue (conditional)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-mirror-baseline-cancellation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-chirality-residue-mass-term","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-archimedean-chirality"],"tags":["delta-lambda","isovector","chirality","bring-surface","conditional"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.binding_isovector_mirror_from_chiral","text":"isovector-chiral-residue.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:isovector-chiral-residue\"></a><p><strong>Conditional on the identification <code>BWVacuumRowIsHecke</code>.</strong>\nLet the bar-odd isovector component of the nuclear binding residual equal the chiral residue of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">W_\\lambda</code> Plancherel measure <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu(\\lambda) = d_q(\\lambda)^2/D^2</code>—that is, the Reeb-involution-odd chiral mass component <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_{\\mathrm{chiral}}</code> (<a href=\"#prop:chirality-residue-mass-term\" data-at=\"mass-theory/plancherel-alpha-spectral\">Chirality residue mass term</a>, <a href=\"#rem:archimedean-chirality\" data-at=\"brings-surface/archimedean-condition-leptons\">Archimedean chirality</a>) coupled to the isovector writhe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2(Z-N)</code> (<a href=\"#prop:mirror-baseline-cancellation\" data-at=\"nuclear-interactions/atomic-braid-mass-crossing-locality-cpt\">Mirror-pair cancellation of the bar-even binding baseline</a>) with chiral weight <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa</code>. Then the isovector mirror difference satisfies</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">b(Z,N) - b(N,Z) \\;=\\; 4\\,\\kappa\\,(Z-N),</code></pre>\n<p>independently of the mass number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = Z+N</code>; equivalently, the per-isospin slope <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b = 4\\kappa</code> is determined without free parameters by the single chiral weight <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/isovector-chiral-residue.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"14.9.10","page":"b/prop-isovector-chiral-residue","lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.binding_isovector_mirror_from_chiral","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/BraidKnotOctonion/BindingIsovectorChiralResidue.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
